WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:06.290
The original 1995 Mortal Kombat film is a
nostalgic cult classic, and its stars remain

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:11.900
the iconic screen portrayals of characters
like Liu Kang, Shang Tsung, and Sonya Blade.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.520
These actors were rewarded with a rare glimpse
into the life of a Hollywood performer, but

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:17.520
where are they now?

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:23.580
Already starring as Connor MacLeod in Highlander,
another fantasy/action franchise, Christopher

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:28.420
Lamber was given top billing for his supporting
role as Lord Raiden in the original Mortal

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:29.650
Kombat film.

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:33.870
Lambert declined to appear in the sequel,
citing scheduling conflicts at the time, though

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:37.680
he later revealed that he simply didn't think
the script was any good.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:43.450
He was succeeded by James Remar of The Warriors
and Dexter fame in Mortal Kombat: Annihilation,

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.999
followed by Tadanobu Asano in the 2021 remake.

00:00:46.999 --> 00:00:52.230
In 2020, Lambert briefly returned to voice
lines for a downloadable skin of the Thunder

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:56.440
God that bears his likeness in the Mortal
Kombat 11 game.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:01.249
While appearing in fewer blockbusters, Lambert
has continued to perform in film and television

00:01:01.249 --> 00:01:06.260
productions across the world, from the French
comedy series Call My Agent! to the Academy

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:09.700
Award-nominated Russian historical drama Sobibor.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:16.009
American audiences most likely saw him last
as Bastien Moreau in a 2019 arc of NBC's The

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:17.009
Blacklist.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:22.630
In addition to acting, Lambert co-owns a vineyard
in Argentina, travels, and customizes automobiles.

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:30.090
The true lead in 1995's Mortal Kombat is Liu
Kang, portrayed by actor and martial artist

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.340
Robin Shou.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:35.749
Mortal Kombat was Shou's first major Hollywood
role, but he brought with him nine years of

00:01:35.749 --> 00:01:39.619
experience as a stunt performer in both Hollywood
and Hong Kong.

00:01:39.619 --> 00:01:44.789
Shou also assisted fight choreographer Pat
E. Johnson in staging some of his martial

00:01:44.789 --> 00:01:49.939
arts battles in Mortal Kombat, and he accepted
the offer to take the lead as fight choreographer

00:01:49.939 --> 00:01:51.009
for the sequel.

00:01:51.009 --> 00:01:57.229
In 1997, Shou both reprised the role of Liu
Kang in Mortal Kombat: Annihilation and played

00:01:57.229 --> 00:02:00.429
Gobei opposite Chris Farley in Beverly Hills
Ninja.

00:02:00.429 --> 00:02:06.389
Shou would reunite with Mortal Kombat director
Paul W.S. Anderson for his 2008 remake of

00:02:06.389 --> 00:02:07.670
Death Race.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:13.550
He also reprised 14K, his character in Death
Race, for the film's first two sequels, Death

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:16.480
Race 2 and Death Race: Inferno.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:21.390
Portraying Gen in 2009's Street Fighter: The
Legend of Chun-Li gave him the rare distinction

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:25.569
of playing both a Mortal Kombat character
and a Street Fighter character.

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:31.290
He also had a small role in the 2006 film
adaptation of DOA: Dead or Alive, giving him

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:34.900
the rare "fighting game movie adaptation"
hat trick.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:40.030
According to a 2020 interview with the podcast
Monsters, Madness and Magic, Shou has since

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:41.989
dedicated himself to parenting.

00:02:41.989 --> 00:02:47.120
"So the last seven years I've been basically
devoted myself to um, raise my kids."

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:52.720
Linden Ashby was just breaking into major
motion pictures when he was cast as Hollywood

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.689
big-shot Johnny Cage.

00:02:54.689 --> 00:02:59.870
Just before Mortal Kombat, he played supporting
roles opposite Kevin Costner and Luke Perry

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:02.650
in Wyatt Earp and 8 Seconds, respectively.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:08.019
On Mortal Kombat, Ashby enjoyed the freedom
to improvise and influence his characterization,

00:03:08.019 --> 00:03:12.000
but he found shooting the fight sequences
to be a punishing experience.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.329
Unhappy with the role he was offered for the
sequel, Ashby declined to return for Mortal

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:18.189
Kombat: Annihilation.

00:03:18.189 --> 00:03:22.659
After Mortal Kombat, he continued to appear
in smaller action films and thrillers throughout

00:03:22.659 --> 00:03:28.989
the 90s and 2000s, but his most famous role
would come in 2011 when he was cast as Sheriff

00:03:28.989 --> 00:03:33.310
Noah Stilinski in MTV's TV remake of Teen
Wolf.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:38.829
Playing the father of one of the lead characters,
Ashby appeared in 88 episodes of the hit series.

00:03:38.829 --> 00:03:43.000
All these years later, however, Ashby hasn't
forgotten his video game days.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:48.860
In 2020, he recorded new voice lines and lent
his likeness to the, quote, "Hollywood Kombatant"

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:51.299
skin for Johnny Cage in Mortal Kombat 11.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:56.940
Cary-Hiroyuki Tagawa is one of those great
recognizable actors.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:02.170
He appeared in action films like Showdown
in Little Tokyo and Rising Sun before becoming

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.750
the villainous Shang Tsung in Mortal Kombat.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:09.989
While only making a brief appearance in Mortal
Kombat: Annihilation, Tagawa is the one original

00:04:09.989 --> 00:04:14.909
actor to reprise a role in the web series
Mortal Kombat: Legacy, appearing in three

00:04:14.909 --> 00:04:16.980
episodes in 2013.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:22.600
He also returned as Shang Tsung in 2019's
Mortal Kombat 11 as the game's canonical version

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:23.820
of Shang Tsung.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:28.510
He is, however, succeeded by Chin Han in the
2021 Mortal Kombat film.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:32.940
Outside of Mortal Kombat, Tagawa has remained
a constant on-screen presence.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:38.190
He had a recurring role on the Netflix reboot
of Lost in Space, and he portrayed Trade Minister

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:43.540
Nobusuke Tagomi on three seasons of Amazon's
The Man in the High Castle.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:48.250
Tagawa has voiced frustrations over the limited
roles available to Asian actors in Hollywood,

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:51.100
which has led to his long tenure playing villains.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:55.740
In a 2006 documentary titled The Slanted Screen,
Tagawa said,

00:04:55.740 --> 00:05:01.390
"If I'm going to choose between a wimpy businessman
and a bad guy, I'm gonna play a bad guy because

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:02.450
I got balls."

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:06.710
Bridgette Wilson had one heck of a 1995.

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:10.980
Only two years into an exciting film career
that began opposite Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:15.770
in Last Action Hero, Wilson ended up starring
in two hit movies in one year.

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:21.010
First, she appeared as third-grade teacher
Veronica Vaughn in Adam Sandler's Billy Madison.

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:25.970
Next, she would win the role of Special Forces
Officer Sonya Blade in Mortal Kombat, which

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:31.040
became available after Cameron Diaz — hot
off her comedy debut in The Mask — broke

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:33.160
her wrist training for the film.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:39.100
Wilson continued to appear in multiple movies
a year, including four feature films in 1997,

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:43.640
which left no room in her schedule for Mortal
Kombat: Annihilation — or so she claimed.

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:48.520
However, Wilson would return to voice the
Klassic MK Movie Sonya Blade skin for Mortal

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:49.960
Kombat 11.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:55.330
Since 2008, Wilson has withdrawn from the
busy life of a Hollywood actor to pursue another

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:58.640
of her lifelong dreams — being a full-time
parent and homemaker.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:05.730
Following a prosperous modeling career, Brooklyn
actress Talisa Soto already had a prominent

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:10.530
role in the blockbuster action film License
to Kill before becoming Outworld's Princess

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:12.590
Kitana in Mortal Kombat.

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:17.820
After the video game adaptation, Soto found
herself cast in a string of infamously bad

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:22.750
films, such as Mortal Kombat: Annihilation,
the direct-to-video adaptation of the pulpy

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:28.320
horror comic Vampirella, and 2002's Ballistic:
Ecks vs. Sever.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:33.990
Since then, she made one more credited acting
appearance in 2009 with La Mission, written

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:37.150
and directed by her brother-in-law, Peter
Bratt.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:41.500
Soto has been out of public life for over
a decade and has given few interviews, but

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:46.520
she can often be seen walking the red carpet
at premieres and award shows with her husband,

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:48.920
actor Benjamin Bratt, with whom she has two
children.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:54.890
In the Mortal Kombat movie, English actor
Trevor Goddard portrayed the smirking mercenary

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:59.070
Kano with an Australian accent that was later
adopted in the game series.

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:01.520
So what's the origin behind that voice?

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:06.550
Well, Goddard spent years in Hollywood claiming
to have been a boxer from Perth, Australia,

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:10.320
which was, according to the Lakeland Ledger,
a total invention.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:14.850
Those rare interviews with Goddard that can
be found online still cling to this fiction,

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:17.910
leaving very little information behind about
his real life.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:23.490
While his film career never took off, Goddard
found a home on the CBS drama JAG as Lieutenant

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:25.300
Commander Mic Brumby.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:30.110
He appeared in 42 episodes of the series alongside
his friend Catherine Bell, whom he met on

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:33.940
the set of the low-budget action film Men
of War in 1994.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:39.150
Sadly, Goddard died in 2003 at the age of
40 from a drug overdose.

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:43.730
His final feature film role, which hit screens
a month later, was Grapple, a pirate aboard

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:47.650
the titular vessel in Pirates of the Caribbean:
The Curse of the Black Pearl.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:53.130
One of the most iconic characters from the
Mortal Kombat video game series, Scorpion

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:57.240
had a minor role in the original film
where he was all but silent, save for his

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.920
famous taunt.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.440
"Get over here!"

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:05.440
Since his only purpose in the film was to
fight, the role was filled by stunt actor

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:10.860
Chris Casamassa, who also doubled as the on-set
trainer for his on-screen opponent, Johnny

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:13.050
Cage actor Linden Ashby.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:18.090
Casamassa reprised Scorpion in Mortal Kombat:
Annihilation and in four episodes of the short-lived

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:21.550
syndicated television series Mortal Kombat:
Konquest.

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:25.970
Other highlights of his stunt career include
doubling as the Caped Crusader for George

00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:31.980
Clooney in 1997's Batman &amp; Robin and coordinating
on Blade the following year.

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:38.430
He is now president and CEO of Red Dragon
Karate, a school founded in 1965 by his father,

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:40.079
Louis D. Casamassa.

00:08:40.079 --> 00:08:43.390
He is also the head instructor at their Glendora,
California location.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:49.600
The man under Sub-Zero's mask was French martial
artist, dancer, and personal trainer François

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:50.600
Petit.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:55.259
Petit was involved in the film long before
the rest of the cast, working to recruit more

00:08:55.259 --> 00:08:56.259
stunt performers.

00:08:56.259 --> 00:09:01.209
When a suitable actor couldn't be found to
play Sub-Zero, the role fell to Petit, though

00:09:01.209 --> 00:09:04.790
his on-set responsibilities led to a reduction
of the part.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:10.110
In addition to his work staging the action,
Petit was also Cary-Hiroyuki Tagawa's fight

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:11.110
trainer.

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:15.230
Petit has personally trained huge stars throughout
his career, including Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:16.560
and Dwayne Johnson.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:21.480
He served on the WWF medical staff in the
'90s and can be seen tending to Mick Foley

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:27.490
after the wrestler's now-famous 16-foot fall
in the, quote, "Hell in a Cell" match at 1998's

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:28.640
King of the Ring event.

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:32.910
While no longer active in Hollywood, Petit
has worked as a dance choreography consultant

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:34.339
as recently as 2020.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:40.630
Master Keith Cooke Hirabayashi was already
a celebrated martial arts competitor before

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:43.610
he began taking roles in Hollywood action
movies.

00:09:43.610 --> 00:09:49.060
In 1990, he appeared opposite martial arts
legend Cynthia Rothrock in the two back-to-back

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:52.660
films China O'Brien and China O'Brien 2.

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:57.490
After initial test screenings for Mortal Kombat
came back with one prevailing request — quote,

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:58.839
"More fights!"

00:09:58.839 --> 00:10:03.480
— Cooke was brought in to participate in
one of the added action sequences as Reptile.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:08.470
Cooke's decades of experience made him a great
dance partner for Robin Shou's Liu Kang.

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:13.579
Cooke was invited back in 1997 for a fighting
and speaking role as the new Sub-Zero in Mortal

00:10:13.579 --> 00:10:18.519
Kombat: Annihilation, and he would also join
Robin Shou in Beverly Hills Ninja that same

00:10:18.519 --> 00:10:19.519
year.

00:10:19.519 --> 00:10:23.389
While he no longer appears in films, he is
the owner and head instructor of Keith Cooke

00:10:23.389 --> 00:10:28.339
Studios in Brentwood, California, where he's
trained several Hollywood stars in preparation

00:10:28.339 --> 00:10:30.579
for athletically demanding roles.

00:10:30.579 --> 00:10:32.889
